WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
1959. In «Les 400 coups»,

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.910
a boy sits answering an adult's questions.

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.090
But the adult stays «hors champ».

4
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.900
We only hear her voice.

5
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.060
The camera stays on the boy.

6
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.020
Why would a director film
a conversation like that?

7
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.050
You could simply tell the story.

8
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.540
So how do you write about the filmmaking,

9
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.310
not a plot summary?

10
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.680
In this mission, you'll open the
film evidence toolbox in Mission D1,

11
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.320
drawer by drawer.

12
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.080
Then you'll climb the three-step
staircase in Mission D2,

13
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.320
using that same interview scene.

14
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: find out how to
write about a film as a film.
